#Hydrological study of the Qb sub-catchment-Cotonou(Benin)

This project presents a hydrological study of the Qb sub-catchment located in the city of Cotonou, Benin, an urba area highly exposed to flooding due to rapid urbanization and increasing soil imperviousness.

The main objective is to estimate runoff peak dischearges generated by extreme rainfall events using frequency analysis of daily maximum rainfall and morphometric characterization of the catchment.

Extreme rainfall was analyzed using statistical distributions (Gumbel, GEV, Normal), with model selection based on information criteria (AIC, BIC). Peak discharges were estimated using the Rational Method and the CIEH method

Tools used
- Global Mapper and ArcGis (watershed delineation)
- QGIS (mapping)
- HYFRAN (frequency analysis)
- Excel and PowerPoint (analysis and presentation)

This repository contains data used, final maps, analysis results and the thesis defense presentation.


